From 8eb9e7f8154db51d796180a947869b5c62543784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] dos: Count client CREATE cells over the circuit
 creation rate

The network team asks whether a circuit flood comes from many addresses
or from a few. DoSCircuitCreation answers only for addresses it marks,
and it marks an address only once its bucket is empty and it holds at
least DoSCircuitCreationMinConnections connections, so addresses that
each keep one connection are never counted, however fast they create
circuits.

Count, as tor_relay_dos_total{type="circuit_over_rate"}, every CREATE
cell from a client channel that finds its address's circuit bucket
empty, whether or not the address is marked. Over an interval, (client
CREATE cells - these) / DoSCircuitCreationRate is a lower bound on how
many client addresses sent CREATE cells, since each address can only
send that many per second within its rate. It counts only while
DoSCircuitCreationEnabled is set, as the bucket does.

Part of #41339.
